# spec: set_anc on from ANC off writes the current step with the enabled byte set twice, because a [1.5] write that switches ANC on ignores its step and recalls the selected preset; the second write sets the step while ANC is on, so CNC ends at the step it had.
# source: hardware report on firmware 1.8.2-11524+e0f7590 with presets 3 4 9 and preset 0 selected: GET [1.5] returned 0b0400, SETGET 0401 returned 0b0301 (the selected preset, not step 4), and a second SETGET 0401 returned 0b0401. Each SETGET was also followed by a STATUS [1.15] 00030409, which the adapters skip.
device nc700
call set_anc on
send 01 05 01 00
recv 01 05 03 03 0b 04 00
send 01 05 02 02 04 01
recv 01 05 03 03 0b 03 01
send 01 05 02 02 04 01
recv 01 05 03 03 0b 04 01
result ok
